e Tex, Marvin Gaye, Al Green, Larry Graham. Las máquinas sustituyeron vientos, órgano (el Yamaha DX7), batería y bajo: solo sobrevivió la guitarra rítmica sobre el bajo sintetizado y la palmada electrónica. La insinuación dejó paso al sexo explícito sin cerebro («Do Me Baby», «Beep a Freak»), y llegaron el bass de Miami (2 Live Crew), Egyptian Lover, el New Jack Swing de Teddy Riley y la farsa de Milli Vanilli. Los funkers de verdad abandonaron la radio: el underground (hip hop, go-go) llevó el funk adelante.","color":"#22d3ee","family":"Funk de los ochenta: Prince, Rick James, electro","link":"https://volteret4.github.io/Funk/#naked-funk"}],"book_tracks":[{"id":5400674955993,"artist":"Sheena Easton","artist_id":259459927005557,"title":"Sugar Walls","year":1984,"ess":0,"yt":"CqH7LlWwIww","kind":null,"book":{"id":4,"title":"Funk: The Music, the People, and the Rhythm of the One","author":"Rickey Vincent","url":"https://volteret4.github.io/Funk/"},"scene":"Naked funk: la era Reagan","scene_id":266579790140761,"scene_link":"https://volteret4.github.io/Funk/#naked-funk","chapters":["Cap. 19: Funk in the 1980s: Super Freaks"],"pages":[[1,271]]}],"mentions":[{"book":"Funk: The Music, the People, and the Rhythm of the One","author":"Rickey Vincent","page":271,"text":"…were forced to compete with lighter, voiceless (and often talentless) wisps that survived on sex appeal alone. Prince protégés Vanity, Appolonia, Sheena Easton, and veteran percussionist Sheila E (Escovedo) all went for the cynical image change. Songs like “Pretty Mess,” “Nasty Girl,” “Sex Shooter,”…"}],"podcast":[],"awards":[{"kind":"award","title":"Grammy Award for Best New Artist (1982)","body":"Nominated.","year":1982,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","episode":null,"url":"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q1453643"}]},{"kind":"award","title":"Grammy Award for Best Mexican/Mexican-American Album (1985) — Me Gustas Tal Como Eres","body":"Won.","year":1985,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Wikidata","epis